ONE CHANGE LANDED AFTER THE GATE CHAINS, and it is named here rather than
quietly folded in: `cargo clippy --all-targets` on aarch64 flags
`vdupq_n_u16((CDEF_VERY_LARGE as u16) ^ 0x8000)` as an unnecessary cast.
`CDEF_VERY_LARGE` is already `u16` (cdef.rs:59), so the cast is a type-level
no-op; the warning was PRE-EXISTING on `cdef_filter_cols8_neon` and this
commit's 4-wide body copied the line, so both were dropped in one edit and
`cdef.rs` is now clippy-clean on aarch64. The full `zenav1-svt-dsp` test suite
(including the eleven `c_parity_cdef` tests) and two of the still reference
cells were re-run afterwards and pass; the byte gates cannot be affected by
removing an identity cast.

=================== MEMORY ===================

Nothing here allocates, and the scratch neither shrinks nor grows: the arm
writes the same `[i32; 32]` the i32 form did. Measured all the same, since the
aarch64 inter arm is where the memory goal is stated. `tools/mem_bisect.sh`
runs both binaries ROUND-ROBIN in one invocation, so box drift lands on both
equally; 11 rounds each, 0 refused, every run encoding (obu 139,761 B inter /
70,893 B still):

    aarch64 peak RSS, gradient 2048x2048 qp 40 preset 13
    arm    build  median KiB   min      max
    inter  base   140,304      138,560  158,928
    inter  cand   140,176      140,144  159,024
    still  base    72,656       72,624   77,136
    still  cand    72,688       72,624   78,448

**Both arms are NULLS** — the distributions overlap completely and the inter
median moves DOWN by 128 KiB (0.09 %). **The aarch64 2048-inter arm, which is
the one the memory ceiling is stated against, is not pushed anywhere.**

=================== WHAT IS AND IS NOT ESTABLISHED ===================

ESTABLISHED: that the 4-wide NEON arm is 1.58-1.67x faster at the kernel, on
six runs with disjoint intervals; that the untouched 8-wide arm is unchanged;
that this box's whole-frame `perf_ab` floor is +-0.4 % and the change is inside
it; that the arm is byte-identical to the scalar core over the full knob domain
and to real C.

NOT ESTABLISHED: any frame-level gain on aarch64 — see above. Also not
measured: any instruction count (callgrind is Linux-only), any preset but 2 and
6, any qp but 40, 10-bit (the HBD arm still runs the i32 `cdef_filter_cols8_neon`),
and the inter arm. And the 8-wide NEON arm still multiplies PER TAP where C
groups by coefficient (`sum += pri_taps[0] * (p0 + p1)`) — twelve `vmulq_s16`
where four would do. That is the same insight `cdef_i16_kernel_2026-09-05`
applied on x86 and it is NOT applied here; it is the obvious next chunk and the
`cdef_filter_block_8x8` bench case now exists to price it.
